YOO-ter"],["phone","das Handy","dahs HEN-dee"],["work","die Arbeit","dee AR-bite"],["office","das Büro","dahs bew-ROH"],["doctor","der Arzt","dair ahrtst"],["police officer","der Polizist","dair poh-li-TSIST"],["lesson","die Stunde","dee SHTOON-deh"],["exam","die Prüfung","dee PREW-foong"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["big","groß","grohs"],["small","klein","kline"],["good","gut","goot"],["bad","schlecht","shlekht"],["new","neu","noy"],["old","alt","ahlt"],["beautiful","schön","shuhn"],["ugly","hässlich","HES-likh"],["fast","schnell","shnel"],["slow","langsam","LAHNG-zahm"],["easy","leicht","lykht"],["difficult","schwer","shvair"],["cheap","billig","BIL-ikh"],["expensive","teuer","TOY-er"],["clean","sauber","ZOW-ber"],["dirty","schmutzig","SHMOOT-sikh"]]},{"id":"common-verbs","title":"Common verbs","items":[["to be","sein","zine"],["to have","haben","HAH-ben"],["to go","gehen","GAY-en"],["to want","wollen","VOL-en"],["to eat","essen","ES-en"],["to drink","trinken","TRIN-ken"],["to speak","sprechen","SHPREKH-en"],["to see","sehen","ZAY-en"],["to come","kommen","KOM-en"],["to give","geben","GAY-ben"],["to know (a fact)","wissen","VIS-en"],["to do / make","machen","MAH-khen"],["to say","sagen","ZAH-gen"],["to like","mögen","MUH-gen"],["to live","wohnen","VOH-nen"],["to work","arbeiten","AR-by-ten"],["to buy","kaufen","KOW-fen"],["to read","lesen","LAY-zen"],["to write","schreiben","SHRY-ben"],["to sleep","schlafen","SHLAH-fen"],["to learn","lernen","LAIR-nen"],["to help","helfen","HEL-fen"],["to need","brauchen","BROW-khen"],["to love","lieben","LEE-ben"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Ich, du, er/sie/es, wir, ihr, sie, and the polite Sie. Sie (capital S) is formal and works for one or many people."],"rows":[["I","ich","ikh"],["you (informal)","du","doo"],["he / she / it","er / sie / es","air / zee / es"],["we","wir","veer"],["you all (informal)","ihr","eer"],["they","sie","zee"],["you (formal)","Sie","zee"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ich bin Student","ikh bin shtoo-DENT"],["you are tall","du bist groß","doo bist grohs"],["she is my sister","sie ist meine Schwester","zee ist MY-neh SHVES-ter"],["we are friends","wir sind Freunde","veer zint FROYN-deh"],["they are teachers","sie sind Lehrer","zee zint LAY-rer"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Plurals are irregular. Learn each noun with its plural. The plural article is always \"die\". Common endings: -e, -en, -er, umlaut, -s, or no change."],"rows":[["der / die / das (plural)","die","dee"],["add -e (often with umlaut)","der Hund → die Hunde","doon-deh"],["add -en","die Frau → die Frauen","FROW-en"],["umlaut, no ending","der Vater → die Väter","FAY-ter"],["add -s (foreign words)","das Auto → die Autos","OW-tohs"]],"ex":[["one dog, two dogs","ein Hund, zwei Hunde","eyn hoont tsvy HOON-deh"],["one woman, women","eine Frau, Frauen","EYE-neh frow FROW-en"],["one book, two books","ein Buch, zwei Bücher","eyn bookh tsvy BEW-kher"],["one car, cars","ein Auto, Autos","eyn OW-toh OW-tohs"],["one child, children","ein Kind, Kinder","eyn kint KIN-der"]]},{"id":"sein-to-be","title":"Sein: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","ich bin","ikh bin"],["you are","du bist","doo bist"],["he / she is","er / sie ist","air / zee ist"],["we are","wir sind","veer zint"],["you all are","ihr seid","eer zide"],["they are / you are (formal)","sie sind / Sie sind","zee zint"]],"ex":[["I am English","ich bin Engländer","ikh bin ENG-len-der"],["he is a doctor","er ist Arzt","air ist ahrtst"],["we are tired","wir sind müde","veer zint MEW-deh"],["are you from Berlin?","bist du aus Berlin?","bist doo ows bair-LEEN"],["they are at home","sie sind zu Hause","zee zint tsoo HOW-zeh"]]},{"id":"haben-to-have","title":"Haben: to have","text":[],"rows":[["I have","ich habe","ikh HAH-beh"],["you have","du hast","doo hahst"],["he / she has","er / sie hat","air / zee haht"],["we have","wir haben","veer HAH-ben"],["you all have","ihr habt","eer hahpt"],["they have","sie haben","zee HAH-ben"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","ich habe einen Bruder","ikh HAH-beh EYE-nen BROO-der"],["she has two cats","sie hat zwei Katzen","zee haht tsvy KAHT-sen"],["we have time","wir haben Zeit","veer HAH-ben tsite"],["do you have a pen?","hast du einen Stift?","hahst doo EYE-nen shtift"],["they have a car","sie haben ein Auto","zee HAH-ben eyn OW-toh"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Take off -en, then add: -e, -st, -t, -en, -t, -en. Example: machen (to do)."],"rows":[["ich","mache","MAH-kheh"],["du","machst","mahkhst"],["er / sie / es","macht","mahkht"],["wir","machen","MAH-khen"],["ihr","macht","mahkht"],["sie / Sie","machen","MAH-khen"]],"ex":[["I live in Berlin","ich wohne in Berlin","ikh VOH-neh in bair-LEEN"],["you work a lot","du arbeitest viel","doo AR-by-test feel"],["she plays football","sie spielt Fußball","zee shpeelt FOOS-bahl"],["we learn German","wir lernen Deutsch","veer LAIR-nen doytsh"],["they buy bread","sie kaufen Brot","zee KOW-fen broht"]]},{"id":"gehen-to-go","title":"Gehen: to go","text":["Going to do something soon: use gehen or the future. Ich gehe schlafen = I am going to sleep."],"rows":[["I go","ich gehe","ikh GAY-eh"],["you go","du gehst","doo gayst"],["he / she goes","er / sie geht","air / zee gayt"],["we go","wir gehen","veer GAY-en"],["they go","sie gehen","zee GAY-en"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","ich gehe zur Schule","ikh GAY-eh tsoor SHOO-leh"],["where are you going?","wohin gehst du?","voh-HIN gayst doo"],["we are going home","wir gehen nach Hause","veer GAY-en nahkh HOW-zeh"],["she is going shopping","sie geht einkaufen","zee gayt EYN-kow-fen"],["let's go!","los geht's!","lohs gayts"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb is always in position 2. Subject, verb, rest. If you start with time or place, the verb stays second, and the subject moves after it."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Ich esse Brot.","ikh ES-eh broht"],["time first","Heute esse ich Brot.","HOY-teh ES-eh ikh broht"],["with a second verb at the end","Ich will Brot essen.","ikh vil broht ES-en"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","ich esse Brot","ikh ES-eh broht"],["today I eat bread","heute esse ich Brot","HOY-teh ES-eh ikh broht"],["I want to eat bread","ich will Brot essen","ikh vil broht ES-en"],["he lives here","er wohnt hier","air vohnt heer"],["we go to school today","wir gehen heute zur Schule","veer GAY-en HOY-teh tsoor SHOO-leh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Use nicht (not) for verbs and adjectives. Use kein (no / not a) for nouns."],"rows":[["not (verb, adjective)","nicht","nikht"],["not a, no","kein / keine","kine / KY-neh"],["nothing","nichts","nikhts"],["nobody","niemand","NEE-mahnt"],["never","nie","nee"]],"ex":[["I do not speak French","ich spreche kein Französisch","ikh SHPREKH-eh kine frahn-TSUH-zish"],["I am not tired","ich bin nicht müde","ikh bin nikht MEW-deh"],["I have no time","ich habe keine Zeit","ikh HAH-beh KY-neh tsite"],["she does not live here","sie wohnt nicht hier","zee vohnt nikht heer"],["I never eat meat","ich esse nie Fleisch","ikh ES-eh nee flysh"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: put the verb first. With a question word: question word, then verb, then subject."],"rows":[["statement","Du sprichst Englisch.","doo shprikhst ENG-lish"],["question","Sprichst du Englisch?","shprikhst doo ENG-lish"],["with question word","Wo wohnst du?","voh vohnst doo"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","sprichst du Englisch?","shprikhst doo ENG-lish"],["is she a doctor?","ist sie Ärztin?","ist zee AIRTS-tin"],["do you have a pen?","hast du einen Stift?","hahst doo EYE-nen shtift"],["are you tired?","bist du müde?","bist doo MEW-deh"],["is it far?","ist es weit?","ist es vite"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","was","vahs"],["who","wer","vair"],["where","wo","voh"],["where to","wohin","voh-HIN"],["where from","woher","voh-HAIR"],["when","wann","vahn"],["why","warum","vah-ROOM"],["how","wie","vee"],["which","welcher","VEL-kher"],["how much / how many","wie viel / wie viele","vee feel / vee FEE-leh"]],"ex":[["what is this?","was ist das?","vahs ist dahs"],["who is she?","wer ist sie?","vair ist zee"],["where do you live?","wo wohnst du?","voh vohnst doo"],["when is the exam?","wann ist die Prüfung?","vahn ist dee PREW-foong"],["why are you late?","warum bist du spät?","vah-ROOM bist doo shpayt"],["how much is it?","wie viel kostet das?","vee feel KOS-tet dahs"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my","mein / meine","mine / MY-neh"],["your (informal)","dein / deine","dine / DY-neh"],["his / its","sein / seine","zine / ZY-neh"],["her","ihr / ihre","eer / EER-eh"],["our","unser / unsere","OON-zer / OON-zer-eh"],["your (formal)","Ihr / Ihre","eer / EER-eh"]],"ex":[["my house","mein Haus","mine hows"],["your friends","deine Freunde","DY-neh FROYN-deh"],["his sister","seine Schwester","ZY-neh SHVES-ter"],["our teacher","unser Lehrer","OON-zer LAY-rer"],["your name (formal)","Ihr Name","eer NAH-meh"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["du / dein / dir for friends. Sie / Ihr / Ihnen for strangers. With Sie, the verb is the same as \"they\" (sie ... -en)."],"rows":[["you, informal","du","doo"],["you, formal","Sie","zee"],["your, informal","dein","dine"],["your, formal","Ihr","eer"],["to you, formal","Ihnen","EE-nen"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","du sprichst","doo shprikhst"],["you speak (formal)","Sie sprechen","zee SHPREKH-en"],["how are you? (informal)","wie geht's dir?","vee gayts deer"],["how are you? (formal)","wie geht es Ihnen?","vee gayt es EE-nen"],["thank you (formal)","vielen Dank, Herr Müller","FEE-len dahnk hair MEW-ler"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Spoken past: haben / sein + past participle (ge-...-t or ge-...-en). Future: werden + infinitive."],"rows":[["I have worked","ich habe gearbeitet","ikh HAH-beh geh-AR-by-tet"],["I have eaten","ich habe gegessen","ikh HAH-beh geh-GES-en"],["I went","ich bin gegangen","ikh bin geh-GAHNG-en"],["I will go","ich werde gehen","ikh VAIR-deh GAY-en"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","gestern habe ich gearbeitet","GES-tern HAH-beh ikh geh-AR-by-tet"],["she bought a book","sie hat ein Buch gekauft","zee haht eyn bookh geh-KOWFT"],["I went home","ich bin nach Hause gegangen","ikh bin nahkh HOW-zeh geh-GAHNG-en"],["I will call you tomorrow","ich rufe dich morgen an","ikh ROO-feh dikh MOR-gen ahn"],["we will eat at eight","wir essen um acht Uhr","veer ES-en oom ahkht oor"]]}],"name":"German","id":"de","badge":"Solid","note":"Starter speaking. Capitals mark the stressed syllable."}